  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: Modifying List
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: "Programs can change existing elements, add new elements, or remove
    elements from a list.\nTo change a value, use the element index. Example:\n<indent=1em><font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\">minerals <color=#D4D4D4>=</color> <color=#D4D4D4\">[</color><color=#CE9178>\"WhiteOre\"</color><color=#D4D4D4\">,</color>
    <color=#CE9178>\"BlackOre\"</color><color=#D4D4D4\">]</color></font>\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\">minerals<color=#D4D4D4\">[</color><color=#B5CEA8>1</color><color=#D4D4D4\">]</color>
    <color=#D4D4D4>=</color> <color=#CE9178>\"PurpleEssence\"</color></font></indent>\n\nThe
    list now contains:\n<indent=2em>- <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#CE9178>\"WhiteOre\"</color></font></indent>\n<indent=2em>-
    <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#CE9178>\"PurpleEssence\"</color></font></indent>\n\nLists
    can also use special list methods. A method is a function that belongs to a specific
    object or data type. List methods allow programs to organize and update data
    dynamically during execution. Methods are called using a dot <font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#D4D4D4>.</color></font> after the variable name.\n\nCommon list
    methods:\n<indent=2em>- <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\">minerals<color=#D4D4D4\">.</color><color=#DBDBAB>append</color><color=#D4D4D4\">(</color><color=#CE9178>\"gear\"</color><color=#D4D4D4\">)</color></font>
    \u2192 Add a new element to the end of the list</indent>\n<indent=2em>- <font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\">minerals<color=#D4D4D4\">.</color><color=#DBDBAB>remove</color><color=#D4D4D4\">(</color><color=#CE9178>\"white_ore\"</color><color=#D4D4D4\">)</color></font>
    \u2192 Remove an element from the list</indent>\n<indent=2em>- <font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\">minerals<color=#D4D4D4\">.</color><color=#DBDBAB>pop</color><color=#D4D4D4\">(</color><color=#B5CEA8>0</color><color=#D4D4D4\">)</color></font>
    \u2192 Remove the element at a specific index</indent>"
  isImageBig: 0
